INSERT INTO `assignment_questions` VALUES (1,13,66,1,'Apply Thevenin\'s theorem to find current through a 5Ω load resistor in a given DC network and verify using Norton\'s equivalent.','descriptive','CO1','Analyze',10,1,0,9,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(2,13,66,1,'A series RL circuit has R=10Ω and L=0.5H. It is connected to a 100V DC supply at t=0. Derive and plot the current response i(t).','descriptive','CO1','Analyze',10,1,0,9,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(3,13,67,1,'A series RLC circuit has R=10Ω, L=0.1H, C=100μF connected to 230V, 50Hz supply. Calculate impedance, current, power factor and draw phasor diagram.','descriptive','CO2','Analyze',10,1,0,9,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(4,13,67,1,'Derive the condition for resonance in a series RLC circuit. Calculate resonant frequency, Q-factor and bandwidth for given values.','descriptive','CO2','Evaluate',10,1,0,9,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(5,13,68,1,'Explain the construction and working of a single-phase transformer. Derive the EMF equation and calculate efficiency at full load with given parameters.','descriptive','CO3','Analyze',10,1,0,9,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(6,13,68,2,'A 10KVA, 2000/200V single-phase transformer has core loss 100W and full load copper loss 200W. Find efficiency at full load and half load at 0.8 pf lagging.','scenario','CO3','Evaluate',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(7,13,69,2,'Explain the working principle of a DC shunt motor. Draw its speed-torque characteristics and explain speed control methods.','descriptive','CO4','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(8,13,69,2,'Explain the construction of a three-phase induction motor. Derive the expression for torque and explain the torque-slip characteristics.','descriptive','CO4','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(9,13,70,2,'Explain the constructional features and working of a single-phase induction motor. Why is it not self-starting and how is it made self-starting?','descriptive','CO5','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(10,13,70,2,'Explain the components of LT switchgear. A house has 5 fans (60W), 8 bulbs (40W) running 10hrs/day. Calculate monthly energy consumption and cost at ₹6/unit.','scenario','CO6','Evaluate',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 13:41:37'),(11,12,56,1,'Construct a diagonal scale to represent km, hectometers and decameters with RF=1/50000. Mark a distance of 3km 4hm 6dm on it.','descriptive','CO1','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(12,12,56,1,'Draw a parabola with focus-directrix distance of 60mm using eccentricity method. Label axis, vertex, focus and directrix.','descriptive','CO1','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(13,12,57,1,'A line AB of 70mm length has its end A 15mm above HP and 20mm in front of VP. The line is inclined at 30° to HP and 45° to VP. Draw projections.','descriptive','CO2','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(14,12,57,1,'Draw the orthographic projections (front view, top view, side view) of an L-shaped object given its pictorial view with all dimensions.','descriptive','CO2','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(15,12,58,1,'Draw the front view and top view of a pentagonal prism (base 30mm, height 60mm) resting on its base with an axis perpendicular to VP.','descriptive','CO3','Analyze',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(16,12,58,2,'A cone of base 50mm diameter and height 70mm is cut by a section plane perpendicular to VP and inclined at 45° to HP. Draw sectional front view and true shape of section.','descriptive','CO3','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(17,12,59,2,'Develop the lateral surface of a cylinder of diameter 40mm and height 60mm. Show the development using CAD.','descriptive','CO4','Evaluate',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(18,12,59,2,'Draw the development of the lateral surface of a pentagonal pyramid with base 30mm and height 60mm using CAD tools.','descriptive','CO4','Evaluate',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(19,12,60,2,'Draw the isometric view of a combination solid (cylinder placed on a rectangular prism) with given orthographic dimensions.','descriptive','CO5','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(20,12,60,2,'Convert the given three orthographic views (front, top, side) of a stepped block into its isometric view using CAD conventions.','descriptive','CO6','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-09 17:02:59'),(52,31,146,1,'Explain Python\'s standard data types with examples: numbers, strings, lists, tuples, sets, and dictionaries. Write a program to demonstrate mutable vs immutable types and show key operations on each.','descriptive','CO1','Apply',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(53,31,146,1,'Explain Python operators: arithmetic, relational, logical, bitwise, assignment, and identity operators with examples. Write a program to demonstrate operator precedence with a complex expression.','descriptive','CO1','Apply',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(54,31,147,1,'Write a Python program to implement linear search and binary search on a list. Compare the time complexity of both algorithms. Use list comprehension to filter elements greater than the mean.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(55,31,147,1,'Explain lambda functions, map(), filter(), and reduce() in Python with examples. Write a program using these functions to process a list of student marks: compute pass percentage, filter distinctions, and find highest mark.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(56,31,148,1,'Design a Python class hierarchy for a banking system: Account -> SavingsAccount, CurrentAccount. Implement deposit, withdraw, and calculate_interest methods. Demonstrate polymorphism and method overriding.','descriptive','CO3','Apply',10,1,0,1,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(57,31,148,2,'Explain abstract classes and interfaces in Python using ABC module. Implement a Shape abstract class with area() and perimeter() abstract methods. Create Circle and Rectangle subclasses and demonstrate duck typing.','descriptive','CO3','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(58,31,149,2,'Write a Python program to read a CSV file containing student records, handle FileNotFoundError and ValueError exceptions, and write students with CGPA > 8.0 to a new file. Use try-except-finally blocks.','descriptive','CO4','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(59,31,149,2,'Explain Python\'s exception handling mechanism. Create custom exceptions for a library management system. Demonstrate raise, except, else, and finally clauses in a book issue/return workflow.','descriptive','CO4','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(60,31,150,2,'Write a Python program using NumPy to: create a 3x3 matrix, compute its determinant and inverse, multiply two matrices, and find eigenvalues. Compare execution speed with pure Python implementation.','descriptive','CO5','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(61,31,150,2,'Use Pandas to analyze a given dataset of student marks: load CSV, handle missing values, compute descriptive statistics, group by branch, and plot a bar chart of average marks using Matplotlib.','descriptive','CO6','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:26:21'),(62,10,21,1,'Solve the ODE: (2xy + y^2)dx + (x^2 + 2xy)dy = 0. Test for exactness, solve, and verify. Also solve dy/dx + y*tan(x) = sec(x) using integrating factor method.','descriptive','CO1','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(63,10,21,1,'A body cools from 80°C to 50°C in 5 minutes in a room at 25°C. Using Newton\'s law of cooling, find the temperature after 10 minutes and the time to cool to 35°C.','descriptive','CO1','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(64,10,22,1,'Solve d^2y/dx^2 - 3dy/dx + 2y = e^(3x) using the method of undetermined coefficients. Also solve d^2y/dx^2 + 4y = tan(2x) using variation of parameters.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(65,10,22,1,'Solve Cauchy-Euler equation x^2 y\'\' - 3xy\' + 4y = x^2 ln(x). Explain the method of reduction to constant coefficient ODE with the substitution x = e^t.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(66,10,23,1,'Find the Laplace transform of f(t) = t^2 * e^(-3t) * cos(2t). Use first and second shifting theorems and apply to solve y\'\' + 3y\' + 2y = e^(-t), y(0)=0, y\'(0)=1.','descriptive','CO3','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(67,10,23,2,'State and prove the convolution theorem for Laplace transforms. Use it to evaluate the inverse Laplace transform of 1/(s^2(s^2+a^2)) and verify with direct method.','descriptive','CO3','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(68,10,24,2,'Find the gradient of phi = x^2*y*z + 4*x*z^2 at the point (1,-2,1). Find the directional derivative in the direction of 2i - j - 2k. Determine if the vector field is irrotational.','descriptive','CO4','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(69,10,24,2,'Show that F = (2xy + z^3)i + x^2 j + 3xz^2 k is a conservative field. Find the scalar potential and evaluate the work done in moving a particle from (1,0,0) to (2,1,3).','descriptive','CO4','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(70,10,25,2,'Verify Green\'s theorem for the integral of (xy + y^2)dx + x^2 dy around the boundary of the region bounded by y=x and y=x^2.','descriptive','CO5','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(71,10,25,2,'Apply Stokes\' theorem to evaluate the surface integral of curl F over the surface S of the paraboloid z = 1 - x^2 - y^2 above xy-plane where F = yi - xj + zxk.','descriptive','CO5','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:29:22'),(72,111,41,1,'State and prove Fermat\'s Little Theorem. Use it to compute 3^100 mod 7. Also apply the Chinese Remainder Theorem to solve: x ” 2(mod 3), x ” 3(mod 5), x ” 2(mod 7).','descriptive','CO1','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(73,111,41,1,'Explain the RSA cryptosystem. Choose suitable primes p=11, q=13, e=7 and demonstrate key generation, encryption of message M=5, and decryption.','descriptive','CO1','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(74,111,42,1,'Define conditional probability and Bayes\' theorem. A factory has 3 machines producing 50%, 30%, 20% of output with defect rates 2%, 3%, 5%. If a defective item is found, find the probability it came from machine 1.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(75,111,42,1,'Define random variable, PMF, and CDF. Find the expected value and variance of a discrete random variable with probability distribution: P(X=x) for x=1,2,3,4,5 as 0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.25, 0.15.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(76,111,43,1,'Explain Binomial and Poisson distributions with their properties. A call center receives on average 4 calls per minute. Find the probability of receiving exactly 6 calls in a minute using Poisson distribution.','descriptive','CO3','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(77,111,43,2,'Explain the Normal distribution and its properties. If X~N(50,16), find P(X>58), P(42<X<58), and the value of x such that P(X<x)=0.95 using standard normal tables.','descriptive','CO3','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(78,111,44,2,'Compute mean, median, mode, standard deviation, and coefficient of variation for the dataset: 12, 15, 18, 22, 14, 19, 23, 17, 21, 20. Interpret the results in terms of central tendency and spread.','descriptive','CO4','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(79,111,44,2,'Compute Karl Pearson\'s correlation coefficient for the given paired data of advertising expenditure and sales. Interpret the result and explain the difference between correlation and causation.','descriptive','CO4','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(80,111,45,2,'Explain Type I and Type II errors in hypothesis testing. Conduct a z-test to check if the mean weight of a sample of 100 students (mean=65kg, SD=5kg) differs significantly from population mean of 63kg at 5% level.','descriptive','CO5','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:30:10'),(81,111,45,2,'Fit a regression line y = a + bx to the given data on study hours and exam scores. Predict the score for 7 hours of study. Compute R-squared and interpret the goodness of fit.','descriptive','CO6','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08