n correlation and causation.','descriptive','CO4','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:33:00'),(90,111,45,2,'Explain Type I and Type II errors in hypothesis testing. Conduct a z-test to check if the mean weight of a sample of 100 students (mean=65kg, SD=5kg) differs significantly from population mean of 63kg at 5% level.','descriptive','CO5','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:33:00'),(91,111,45,2,'Fit a regression line y = a + bx to the given data on study hours and exam scores. Predict the score for 7 hours of study. Compute R-squared and interpret the goodness of fit.','descriptive','CO6','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:33:00'),(92,114,206,1,'Explain the types of machine learning: supervised, unsupervised, semi-supervised, and reinforcement learning with real-world examples. Describe the general ML pipeline from data collection to model deployment.','descriptive','CO1','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(93,114,206,1,'Explain bias-variance tradeoff in machine learning. Define overfitting and underfitting. Describe regularization techniques (L1 and L2) and cross-validation methods to address these problems.','descriptive','CO1','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(94,114,207,1,'Derive the cost function and gradient descent update rule for linear regression. Apply simple linear regression to predict house prices given area and price data. Compute MSE and R-squared.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(95,114,207,1,'Explain logistic regression for binary classification. Derive the sigmoid function and log-loss cost function. Apply logistic regression to classify emails as spam (1) or not-spam (0) with given features.','descriptive','CO2','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(96,114,208,1,'Explain the decision tree learning algorithm. Build a decision tree using ID3 algorithm on a small weather dataset. Calculate information gain for each attribute and determine the root node.','descriptive','CO3','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(97,114,208,2,'Explain the Random Forest algorithm. Compare it with a single decision tree in terms of accuracy, overfitting, and interpretability. Describe bagging and feature randomness in random forests.','descriptive','CO3','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(98,114,209,2,'Explain the k-Means clustering algorithm. Apply it to cluster the given 2D dataset with k=3. Show all iterations until convergence, draw cluster boundaries, and discuss the choice of k using elbow method.','descriptive','CO4','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(99,114,209,2,'Explain Principal Component Analysis (PCA) for dimensionality reduction. Apply PCA to a given 4-feature dataset and project to 2 dimensions. Interpret the explained variance ratio.','descriptive','CO4','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(100,114,210,2,'Explain the architecture of a multi-layer perceptron (MLP). Describe forward propagation and backpropagation with chain rule. Trace one complete forward and backward pass for a network with 2 inputs, 2 hidden nodes, and 1 output.','descriptive','CO5','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(101,114,210,2,'Explain the concept of a confusion matrix, precision, recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC. Compute these metrics for a given binary classifier output. Discuss when to prioritize precision vs recall.','descriptive','CO6','Evaluate',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:10'),(102,476,1061,1,'Define an intelligent agent. Describe the five types of agents: simple reflex, model-based, goal-based, utility-based, and learning agents. Give a real-world example for each type.','descriptive','CO1','Analyze',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:35'),(103,476,1061,1,'Explain BFS and DFS for state space search. Apply both to solve the 8-puzzle problem from initial state [[1,2,3],[4,0,5],[6,7,8]] to goal state [[0,1,2],[3,4,5],[6,7,8]]. Compare time and space complexity.','descriptive','CO1','Apply',10,1,0,0,'2026-07-11 08:35:35'),(104,476,1062,1,'Explain A* search algorithm with heuristic f