al ceramic coupling capacitors','The cross-sectional copper thickness of the printed circuit board traces','The input signal source impedance matches','A',0),(10383,4,63,'mcq','To achieve maximum symmetrical peak-to-peak output signal swing without clipping, where should the Q-point reside?',NULL,NULL,'Remember',1,0,'2026-07-09 09:18:57','In the exact center of the active region on the DC load line','Right at the origin point where voltage and current equal zero','Deep within the structural cut-off region boundary','Beyond the maximum collector-emitter breakdown voltage line','A',0),(10384,4,63,'fib','Self-bias is an alternative technical nomenclature for a standard ______ divider bias configuration.',NULL,'voltage','Remember',1,0,'2026-07-09 09:18:57',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0),(10385,4,63,'fib','Unchecked thermal runaway in an uncompensated circuit can ultimately cause the physical ______ of the BJT.',NULL,'destruction','Understand',1,0,'2026-07-09 09:18:57',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0),(10386,4,63,'fib','The DC load line is constructed by plotting two extreme operating points: ideal saturation current and ideal cut-off ______.',NULL,'voltage','Understand',1,0,'2026-07-09 09:18:57',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0),(10387,4,63,'fib','The stability factor S measures the exact rate of change of collector current with respect to changes in reverse saturation ______.',NULL,'current','Remember',1,0,'2026-07-09 09:18:57',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0),(10388,4,63,'fib','In a voltage divider bias circuit, the emitter resistor introduces negative ______ to counter thermal drift.',NULL,'feedback','Understand',1,0,'2026-07-09 09:18:57',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0),(10389,4,63,'fib','A lower numerical value for an operating point stability factor indicates ______ stabilization performance.',NULL,'better','Understand',1,0,'2026-07-09 09:18:57',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0),(10390,4,63,'fib','The quiescent state point of a transistor circuit is universally referred to as the ______ point.